Use symmetry to evaluate $\int_{-\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{6}}\cos 3x\,dx$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=2.6cm, y=1.6cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=-0.5236:0.5236, variable=\x] (-0.5236,0) -- plot ({\x},{cos(deg(3*\x))}) -- (0.5236,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.3,0) -- (1.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.7) -- (0,1.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.05:1.05, smooth, samples=160, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{cos(deg(3*\x))});
\node[below left] at (-0.5236,0) {$-\frac{\pi}{6}$};
\node[below right] at (0.5236,0) {$\frac{\pi}{6}$};
\node[left] at (0,1) {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The function $f$ is even, and $\int_{-3}^{3} f(x)\,dx = 20$.
Find $\int_{0}^{3} f(x)\,dx$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.8cm, y=0.62cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=-3:3, variable=\x] (-3,0) -- plot ({\x},{4-0.3*\x*\x}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-4.6,0) -- (4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.4) -- (0,6.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.9:3.9, smooth, samples=120, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{4-0.3*\x*\x});
\node[below left] at (-3,0) {$-3$};
\node[below right] at (3,0) {$3$};
\node[right] at (1.6,4.6) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

